Ikna (the website at william-lindberg.github.io/ikna, the Android app, their
code, sample decks, texts, icons and other content, together "the Software")
is free to use, but it is not open source. The source code is not published.
The Software is made only to be used: the website to be visited and used, and
the Android app (APK) to be downloaded from the official page and installed.

1. What you may do

   Free of charge, you may:
   a. use the website, and download the Android app from the official page
      (github.com/William-Lindberg/ikna) and install it on your own devices,
      for your own personal, non-commercial learning;
   b. use it in non-commercial teaching, for example a teacher using Ikna with
      a class, as long as nobody is charged for access to Ikna itself;
   c. make backups of your own Ikna data, and share the cards and decks you
      made yourself.

2. What you may not do

