      the copies made automatically when you install, run or visit it yourself;
   b. modify, decompile, reverse engineer or take apart the Software, or make,
      publish or distribute anything based on it (a "derivative work"),
      including a renamed or rebranded version;
   c. use the Software, or any part of it, for commercial purposes. This
      includes selling it, charging for access to it, including it in a paid
      product or service, showing ads in or around it, or using it to make
      money in any other way;
   d. remove or change this license or any copyright notice;
   e. use the name "Ikna" or the Ikna icon for another product.

3. Third-party libraries

   Ikna includes some third-party open-source libraries. Each of them is
